From c9845920bf3c6f27177491f2f21a79ca58459848 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W1nkelm4nn <mrmarkap61@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:10:15 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: Support transform feedback through geometry shaders

Expose VK_EXT_transform_feedback for pipelines that capture from a
geometry shader, which is how DXVK implements D3D11 stream output. poly
already lowers the capture: its rasterization VS writes the vertices, a
count program and a pre-GS program place the primitives. Keep those
programs, run them before the GS compute pass while transform feedback
is active, and implement the buffer bindings, the counters and
vkCmdDrawIndirectByteCountEXT.

poly emits a dummy primitive for invocations without output when the GS
has side effects. Its vertices are shaded as well, so bound the capture
by the primitives of each invocation, or they overwrite the next
invocation's.

Capture from the vertex or tessellation evaluation shader and transform
feedback queries are not supported yet.

Generated-by: LLM
